rts":[{"text":"இரவலர்","lemma":"இரவலர்","gloss":"suppliants"}],"gloss":"suppliants"},{"surface":"வரையா","parts":[{"text":"வரையா","lemma":"வரையா","gloss":"without limiting"}],"gloss":"without limiting","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"வள்ளியோர்","parts":[{"text":"வள்ளியோர்","lemma":"வள்ளியோர்","gloss":"generous patrons"}],"gloss":"generous patrons"},{"surface":"கடைத்தலை","parts":[{"text":"கடை","lemma":"கடை","gloss":"gate"},{"text":"தலை","lemma":"தலை","gloss":"place"}],"gloss":"at the gateway"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஞாங்கர்","parts":[{"text":"ஞாங்கர்","lemma":"ஞாங்கர்","gloss":"there"}],"gloss":"there"},{"surface":"நெடுமொழி","parts":[{"text":"நெடு","lemma":"நெடு","gloss":"long"},{"text":"மொழி","lemma":"மொழி","gloss":"words"}],"gloss":"boastful words"},{"surface":"பயிற்றித்","parts":[{"text":"பயிற்று","lemma":"பயிற்று","gloss":"utter repeatedly"},{"text":"இ","lemma":"இ","gloss":"past participle"},{"text":"த்","lemma":"த்","gloss":"doubled consonant"}],"gloss":"uttering repeatedly"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"தோன்றல்","parts":[{"text":"தோன்றல்","lemma":"தோன்றல்","gloss":"sounding"}],"gloss":"sounding"},{"surface":"செல்லாது","parts":[{"text":"செல்","lemma":"செல்","gloss":"go"},{"text":"ஆது","lemma":"ஆது","gloss":"negative participle"}],"gloss":"not sounding"},{"surface":"என்","parts":[{"text":"என்","lemma":"என்","gloss":"my"}],"gloss":"my"},{"surface":"சிறுகிணைக்","parts":[{"text":"சிறு","lemma":"சிறு","gloss":"small"},{"text":"கிணை","lemma":"கிணை","gloss":"kinai drum"},{"text":"க்","lemma":"க்","gloss":"doubled consonant"}],"gloss":"small kinai drum"},{"surface":"குரலே","parts":[{"text":"குரல்","lemma":"குரல்","gloss":"sound"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"the sound indeed"}]}],"literal":"Sky expanse passed sun's / fresh rays faded reddening-bending twilight / small-very born after tightly-bound / torn leather-strap-my tadari-drum holding / bards eating measure I his / new-wealth good-house granary near stood / blinked opened-eyes measure suddenly / east rising moon dense-darkness to-remove / old-known not-coming form-with my waist / ancient-occurring holes-with thick-thread worn-out / frayed-edges worn-out-my garment-also looking / guest pitiable-one this-man thinking noble-lord / standing music-playing removing greatly / snake-angry-like toddy-with roasted-meat-giving / hell-like my poverty-removed indeed / night-in indeed gave-he my-father / that-day-with today-than beyond / to-beg I-do-not-think poverty-occurring raft-like / mind-with measuring shining nature-I / full-tank sluice-gate-like rejoiced-having-become / one-day suppliants without-limiting generous-patrons gate-place / there boastful-words uttering-repeatedly / sounding not-going my small-kinai-drum sound-indeed","translation":"When the sun had crossed the expanse of the sky and its fresh rays faded into the curving red twilight, just as night began, I held my tadari drum with its tightly bound, torn leather straps. At the hour when bards usually eat, I stood near the granary of his prosperous, good house. In the blink of an eye, as suddenly as that, the moon rose in the east to dispel the dense darkness. Looking at my waist, at my worn-out garment with ancient holes and thick threads, frayed at the edges, making me unrecognizable to those who knew me of old, the noble lord thought, 'He is a guest, worthy of pity.' He stopped the music that was playing, and gave me toddy as fierce as an angry snake along with roasted meat, completely removing my hellish poverty. He, my father, gave this to me in the very night! From that day to this, and even beyond, I do not think of begging. Like a raft that saves one from drowning in poverty, my mind is filled with joy, like a full tank overflowing through its sluice gate. No longer do I stand at the gates of other generous patrons who give without limit, uttering boastful words; the sound of my small kinai drum does not go there anymore.","modern":"வானத்தைக் கடந்து சென்ற சூரியனின் கதிர்கள் மங்கி, சிவந்த அந்திப் பொழுது தோன்றிய இரவின் தொடக்கத்தில், கிழிந்த வாரினைக் கொண்ட என் தடாரிப் பறையைக் கட்டிக்கொண்டு, பாணர்கள் உண்ணும் நேரத்தில், அவனுடைய வளமான நல்ல வீட்டின் நெற்களஞ்சியத்தின் அருகே நின்றேன். இமைத்து விழிக்கும் நேரத்திற்குள், கிழக்கே சந்திரன் தோன்றி இருளை அகற்றியது. பழைய நண்பர்களும் அடையாளம் காண முடியாதபடி, பழமையான துளைகளும் தடித்த நூல்களும் கொண்ட என் கிழிந்த ஆடையை அந்த வள்ளல் நோக்கினான். 'இவன் வறியவன், நம் விருந்தினன்' என்று கருதி, அங்கு நடந்து கொண்டிருந்த இசையை நிறுத்திவிட்டு, கோபமடைந்த பாம்பைப் போன்ற வீரியமிக்க கள்ளையும் சுட்ட இறைச்சியையும் தந்து, நரகத்தைப் போன்ற என் வறுமையைப் போக்கினான். என் தந்தையாகிய அவன் அன்றிரவே எனக்கு இவற்றை வழங்கினான். அன்று முதல் இன்று வரை, இனிமேலும் நான் பிறரிடம் இரந்து நிற்பதை நினைக்க மாட்டேன். வறுமையைக் கடக்கும் புணையைப் போல என் நெஞ்சம் மகிழ்ந்தது. நிறைந்த குளத்தின் மதகு நீர் பாய்வது போல மகிழ்ச்சி அடைந்தேன். நாள்தோறும் இரவலர்க்கு எல்லையின்றி வாரி வழங்கும் பிற வள்ளல்களின் வாயிலில் நின்று, என் புகழுரைகளைக் கூறி, என் சிறு கிணைப் பறையை இனி நான் இசைக்க வேண்டியதில்லை.","explanation":"This poem belongs to the Pāṭāṇ tiṇai (praise of a patron's power and generosity) and the Iyaṉmoḻi tuṟai (extolling the natural excellence and deeds of a patron). The poet Puṟattiṇai Naṉṉākaṉār praises the king Oymāṉ Nalliyāthaṉ for his immediate and overwhelming generosity. The poet describes arriving at the patron's palace at twilight, dressed in rags so worn that he was unrecognizable. The patron immediately recognized his plight, stopped the ongoing court music, and personally served him strong toddy and roasted meat, instantly dispelling his hellish poverty. The poet rejoices that this single act of kindness has freed him from the need to beg at any other patron's gate ever again, comparing his overflowing joy to a full tank releasing water through its sluice gate.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.4],[0.4,0.8],[0.8,1.2],[1.2,1.4],[1.4,2.9],[2.9,3.3],[3.3,4.0],[4.0,4.4],[4.4,5.1],[5.1,5.8],[5.8,6.31],[6.44,6.7],[6.7,8.2],[8.2,8.9],[8.9,9